 built in two separate stages in 1896 and 1906. The museum is an interesting starting point to discover the multi-ethnic background of George Town. Two floors display the history of the immigrant…"],["Penang Time Tunnel Museum","sight",5.42221,100.33954,"39 Green Hall","Mon-Fri 9:15AM-6PM; Sat Sun and public holidays: 9:15AM-6:30PM","","","","r","An interactive museum that features three-dimensional artwork about Penang's history."],["The Roman Catholic Museum Diocese of Penang","sight",5.4206,100.3381,"3 Farquahar Street","Mon-Fri 10AM-5PM; Sat 9AM-1PM","","","","r","The ground floor presents the origin of Catholicism in the Far East in general and in Penang in particular. It also informs about the activities of the diocese of Penang and the ethnic makeup of its members. The first floor exhibits…"],["Church of the Assumption","sight",5.42071,100.33779,"3 Farquhar Street","Mon-Fri 9AM-5PM, Sat 9AM-6PM, Sun 9AM-1PM","","","","r","The first permanent Catholic church to be built in George Town, the Church of the Assumption was established by a group of Eurasian immigrants who accompanied Captain Francis Light to Penang. It is also one of the few churches in…"],["Penang Bowl","activity",5.42377,100.33374,"38-B Farquhar Street","10AM-1AM","","","","r","A 16-lane bowling venue for bowlers within the city centre."],["Sri Wangi Selera Ibunda","restaurant",5.42047,100.33418,"98 Jalan Mutri","from 4PM","","","","r","Serving Sri Lankan and western food. Also home to the Penang Hash House Harriers chapter. In the later-earlier hours it becomes a bar and place where the regulars and travellers hang out."],["Red Garden Cafe","restaurant",5.42098,100.33439,"20, Lebuh Leith","early morning till late","","","","r","Local food: satay, roasted and BBQ'd chicken, duck and pork variations with noodles or rice (Chinese stall in the right corner). Also Thai, Filipino, western and fusion food."],["New World Park Food City","restaurant",5.4203,100.32689,"1, Jalan Burma","","","","","r","Local specialities including curry mee, prawn mee, laksa, chee cheong and fun. For dessert try the ais kacang special with ice cream on top."],["Bibik's Kitchen Nyonya Cuisine","restaurant",5.42157,100.33157,"73, Jalan Sri Bahari","","","","","r","Nyonya restaurant"],["Zen Xin Vegetarian Restaurant","restaurant",5.42096,100.32588,"42, Jalan Nagor","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["The Garage","bar",5.42294,100.33552,"2 Penang Rd","","","","","r","Once owned by the Wearne Brothers, the Garage used to be a motorcar showroom and has since been restored to its Art Deco glory, housing clubs, bars and boutiques."],["MOIS Dance Club","bar",5.42207,100.33585,"Wisma Boon Siew","9PM-3AM","","","","r","A club for the younger crowd in a grand colonial-style building."],["Soho Freehouse","bar",5.42187,100.33383,"50, Ground & Upper Floor, Penang Road,","","","","","r","Selection of continental food and beer. Good place for gaming with pool tables and foosball."]]}